[2026-01-30T16:02:13.709Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Implement interactive contradiction explorer with claim comparison, resolution suggestions, and confidence impact analysis\n\n## Context Area\nTrust & Confidence Visualizations\n\n## Description\nImplement interactive contradiction explorer with claim comparison, resolution suggestions, and confidence impact analysis\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Interactive Contradiction Explorer & Resolution System\n\n### Vision\nBuild an interactive tool for exploring and resolving contradictions found in research. Visualize conflicting claims side-by-side, suggest resolution strategies, show how resolving contradictions affects overall confidence, and track resolution history.\n\n### Business Value\n- Contradictions are critical to research quality\n- Interactive exploration enables informed decisions\n- Resolution suggestions accelerate analysis\n- Confidence impact shows consequence of choices\n- Differentiates from basic contradiction lists\n\n### Scope\n**Included:**\n- Side-by-side claim comparison view\n- Source quality comparison for each claim\n- AI-suggested resolution strategies\n- Confidence impact simulation (what-if)\n- Contradiction severity classification\n- Resolution tracking and history\n- Claim evidence linking\n- Resolution voting for team decisions\n- Export contradiction analysis report\n- Filter by resolution status\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Automatic contradiction resolution\n- External fact-checking API integration\n\n### Key Components\n1. **ContradictionExplorer** - Main container with list and detail view\n2. **ClaimComparison** - Side-by-side conflicting claims\n3. **SourceQualityCompare** - Compare backing sources\n4. **ResolutionSuggester** - AI-powered resolution strategies\n5. **ConfidenceImpactSim** - What-if analysis for resolutions\n6. **SeverityClassifier** - Visual severity indicators\n7. **ResolutionTracker** - Resolution status and history\n8. **EvidenceLinkPanel** - Supporting evidence for each claim\n9. **ResolutionVoting** - Team decision-making UI\n\n### Technical Approach\n- LLM for resolution suggestions (structured output)\n- Confidence propagation algorithm for impact simulation\n- Severity scoring based on source quality diff, claim importance\n- LocalStorage for resolution drafts\n- Supabase for persisted resolutions\n- Real-time updates for team voting\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/ContradictionExplorer.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/ClaimComparison.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/SourceQualityCompare.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/ResolutionSuggester.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/ConfidenceImpactSim.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/contradictions/ResolutionTracker.tsx`\n- Create: `src/lib/contradictionResolution.ts`\n- Create: `src/hooks/useContradictionExplorer.ts`\n- Create: API route: `src/app/api/contradictions/resolve/route.ts`\n- Modify: ContradictionMatrix.tsx - Link to explorer\n\n### Success Criteria\n- Claims compare clearly side-by-side\n- Source quality diff highlights credibility gap\n- AI suggestions are actionable and relevant\n- Impact simulation shows confidence changes\n- Severity accurately reflects importance\n- Resolutions persist across sessions\n- Team voting reflects in real-time\n\n### Potential Challenges\n- AI resolution quality and relevance\n- Confidence propagation complexity\n- Real-time voting synchronization\n- Handling deeply nested contradictions\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"371a1488-aa50-4c52-a397-c861e03f1a24","isSynthetic":true}
